/-!
# The shuffle module of the type-A Hecke algebra

Let `U` be a module over the Hecke algebra `H_l = TypeAHeckeAlgebra R q l`, given by an algebra map
`ρ : H_l →ₐ[R] Module.End R U`. A *mask* is a `k`-element subset of the `k + l` positions
(`TauCeti.TypeAHeckeAlgebra.ShuffleMask k l`); its elements are the *selected* positions and the
other `l` positions are the *rest*. The shuffle module `Sh_k(U)` is the module `ShuffleMask k l → U`
of `U`-valued functions on masks, that is, the free module on the masks tensored with `U`. The
generator `T i` of the Hecke algebra on `k + l` strands crosses the positions `i` and `i + 1`, and
its action depends on which of them are selected:

* if both are selected, it multiplies by `q`;
* if both are rest positions, it acts on `U` by the generator `T r` of `H_l`, where `r` is the index
  of position `i` among the rest positions (`TauCeti.TypeAHeckeAlgebra.ShuffleMask.restIndex`);
* on the two masks `S` (selected, rest) and `S'` (rest, selected) that differ by exchanging the two
  positions, it acts by the symmetric matrix `[[q - q⁻¹, -1], [-1, 0]]`.

These operators satisfy the quadratic, braid and distant-commutation relations of the Hecke
algebra over every commutative ring and for every unit `q`, which gives the representation
`TauCeti.TypeAHeckeAlgebra.shuffleRep k ρ`. In the normalization `gᵢ = q • T i`, so that
`(gᵢ + 1) * (gᵢ - Q) = 0` with `Q = q ^ 2`, two selected positions give the scalar `Q`, and the
mixed block is `[[Q - 1, -q], [-q, 0]]`, the block of the signed checked R-matrix
`TauCeti.signedCheckedR` on two letters `selected < rest`.

The functions supported at the initial mask `{0, …, k - 1}` form a copy of `U` on which the
generators crossing two selected positions act by `q` and the generators crossing two rest
positions act through `ρ`. So this copy is stable under the parabolic subalgebra generated by the
first `k - 1` and the last `l - 1` generators, and is the module `triv_k ⊗ U` of that subalgebra.
The construction is natural in `U`.

The shuffle module is generated by this initial copy of `U`
(`TauCeti.TypeAHeckeAlgebra.span_range_shuffleRep_single_initial_eq_top`). The *length* of a
mask (`TauCeti.TypeAHeckeAlgebra.ShuffleMask.length`) counts the pairs of a rest position and a
later selected position. A *shuffle path* to a mask `S`
(`TauCeti.TypeAHeckeAlgebra.ShuffleMask.IsShufflePath`) is a word `i₁ ⋯ iₘ` in the generator
indices such that, starting from the initial mask, each letter, from the last to the first, moves
a selected position past the rest position after it. Every mask is reached by a shuffle path, and
every shuffle path to `S` has `S.length` letters. Along a shuffle path to `S`:

* the product `T i₁⁻¹ ⋯ T iₘ⁻¹` sends the vector `u` at the initial mask exactly to
  `(-1) ^ S.length • u` at `S`;
* the product `T i₁ ⋯ T iₘ` sends it to a function whose value at `S` is `(-1) ^ S.length • u` and
  which vanishes at every other mask of length at least `S.length`.

In the normalization `gᵢ = q • T i` the leading coefficient is `(-q) ^ S.length`. These are the
surjectivity and triangularity halves of the comparison of the shuffle module with the induced
module `Ind (triv_k ⊗ U)` of the Hecke algebra on `k + l` strands, along the map sending `h ⊗ u` to
`h` applied to `u` at the initial mask. The induced module itself, and the parabolic coset basis
over the subalgebra of the first `k - 1` and the last `l - 1` generators that makes this map an
isomorphism, are not constructed here.

## Main definitions

* `TauCeti.TypeAHeckeAlgebra.ShuffleMask`: the `k`-element subsets of the `k + l` positions.
* `TauCeti.TypeAHeckeAlgebra.ShuffleMask.restIndex`: the number of rest positions before a position.
* `TauCeti.TypeAHeckeAlgebra.shuffleRep`: the shuffle module `Sh_k(U)`.
* `TauCeti.TypeAHeckeAlgebra.ShuffleMask.length`: the length of a mask.
* `TauCeti.TypeAHeckeAlgebra.ShuffleMask.IsShufflePath`: the words moving the initial mask to a
  given mask one selected position at a time.

## Main results

* `TauCeti.TypeAHeckeAlgebra.shuffleRep_T_apply_of_mem_of_mem`,
  `TauCeti.TypeAHeckeAlgebra.shuffleRep_T_apply_of_mem_of_notMem`,
  `TauCeti.TypeAHeckeAlgebra.shuffleRep_T_apply_of_notMem_of_mem` and
  `TauCeti.TypeAHeckeAlgebra.shuffleRep_T_apply_of_notMem_of_notMem`: the action of a generator.
* `TauCeti.TypeAHeckeAlgebra.compLeft_comp_shuffleRep`: naturality in the module `U`.
* `TauCeti.TypeAHeckeAlgebra.shuffleRep_T_single_initial_of_lt` and
  `TauCeti.TypeAHeckeAlgebra.shuffleRep_T_add_single_initial`: the copy of `triv_k ⊗ U` at the
  initial mask.
* `TauCeti.TypeAHeckeAlgebra.ShuffleMask.exists_isShufflePath` and
  `TauCeti.TypeAHeckeAlgebra.ShuffleMask.IsShufflePath.length_eq`: every mask is reached by a
  shuffle path, of the length of the mask.
* `ShuffleMask.IsShufflePath.shuffleRep_prod_val_inv_unitT_single_initial`: the inverse generators
  along a shuffle path act monomially on the initial mask.
* `ShuffleMask.IsShufflePath.shuffleRep_prod_T_single_initial_apply_self` and
  `ShuffleMask.IsShufflePath.shuffleRep_prod_T_single_initial_apply_of_length_le`: the
  generators along a shuffle path act triangularly, with leading coefficient `(-1) ^ S.length`.
* `TauCeti.TypeAHeckeAlgebra.span_range_shuffleRep_single_initial_eq_top`: the shuffle module
  is generated by the initial mask.

## References

* R. Dipper and G. James, *Representations of Hecke algebras of general linear groups*,
  Proc. London Math. Soc. (3) 52 (1986), 20–52, for the Hecke-algebra modules induced from
  parabolic subalgebras, indexed by the cosets of `S_k × S_l` in `S_(k+l)`, that is, by masks.
-/

public section

open Finset

namespace TauCeti.TypeAHeckeAlgebra

variable {k l : ℕ}

/-- The masks of the shuffle module: the `k`-element subsets of the `k + l` positions. The
positions in a mask are *selected*, the other `l` positions are the *rest*. -/
abbrev ShuffleMask (k l : ℕ) : Type := {S : Finset (Fin (k + l)) // #S = k}

namespace ShuffleMask

/-- The mask obtained by exchanging the positions `a` and `b`. -/
def swap (a b : Fin (k + l)) (S : ShuffleMask k l) : ShuffleMask k l :=
  ⟨S.1.map (Equiv.swap a b).toEmbedding, by rw [card_map, S.2]⟩

/-- A position lies in the exchanged mask exactly when its image under the exchange lies in the
original mask. -/
@[simp]
theorem mem_swap {a b x : Fin (k + l)} {S : ShuffleMask k l} :
    x ∈ (S.swap a b).1 ↔ Equiv.swap a b x ∈ S.1 := by
  simp [swap, mem_map_equiv]

/-- Exchanging the same two positions twice gives back the mask. -/
@[simp]
theorem swap_swap (a b : Fin (k + l)) (S : ShuffleMask k l) : (S.swap a b).swap a b = S :=
  Subtype.ext <| Finset.ext fun x ↦ by simp

/-- The number of rest positions of `S` before the position `p`. If `p` is a rest position,
it is the index of `p` among the rest positions, counted from `0`. -/
def restIndex (S : ShuffleMask k l) (p : Fin (k + l)) : ℕ := #{x ∈ S.1ᶜ | x < p}

/-- `S.restIndex p` counts the rest positions of `S` before `p`. -/
theorem restIndex_def (S : ShuffleMask k l) (p : Fin (k + l)) :
    S.restIndex p = #{x ∈ S.1ᶜ | x < p} := (rfl)

/-- A selected position does not change the number of rest positions before it. -/
theorem restIndex_of_mem {S : ShuffleMask k l} {a b : Fin (k + l)} (hab : (b : ℕ) = a + 1)
    (ha : a ∈ S.1) : S.restIndex b = S.restIndex a := by
  unfold restIndex
  congr 1
  ext x
  simp only [mem_filter, mem_compl, Fin.lt_def, hab]
  constructor
  · rintro ⟨hx, hxb⟩
    refine ⟨hx, lt_of_le_of_ne (by omega) fun h ↦ hx ?_⟩
    rwa [show x = a from Fin.ext h]
  · rintro ⟨hx, hxa⟩
    exact ⟨hx, by omega⟩

/-- A rest position adds one to the number of rest positions before the next position. -/
theorem restIndex_of_notMem {S : ShuffleMask k l} {a b : Fin (k + l)} (hab : (b : ℕ) = a + 1)
    (ha : a ∉ S.1) : S.restIndex b = S.restIndex a + 1 := by
  unfold restIndex
  rw [← card_insert_of_notMem (s := {x ∈ S.1ᶜ | x < a}) (a := a) (by simp)]
  congr 1
  ext x
  simp only [mem_filter, mem_compl, mem_insert, Fin.lt_def, hab]
  constructor
  · rintro ⟨hx, hxb⟩
    rcases Nat.lt_succ_iff_lt_or_eq.1 hxb with h | h
    · exact Or.inr ⟨hx, h⟩
    · exact Or.inl (Fin.ext h)
  · rintro (rfl | ⟨hx, hxa⟩)
    · exact ⟨ha, by omega⟩
    · exact ⟨hx, by omega⟩

/-- Exchanging two positions on the same side of `p` does not change the number of rest
positions before `p`. -/
theorem restIndex_swap {S : ShuffleMask k l} {a b p : Fin (k + l)} (h : a < p ↔ b < p) :
    (S.swap a b).restIndex p = S.restIndex p := by
  unfold restIndex
  rw [← card_map (Equiv.swap a b).toEmbedding]
  congr 1
  ext x
  have hx : Equiv.swap a b x < p ↔ x < p := by
    rw [Equiv.swap_apply_def]
    split_ifs with h₁ h₂ <;> subst_vars <;> tauto
  simp [mem_map_equiv, hx]

/-- Two rest positions at or after `p` leave room after the rest positions before `p`. -/
theorem restIndex_add_two_le {S : ShuffleMask k l} {a b p : Fin (k + l)} (hab : a < b)
    (hpa : p ≤ a) (ha : a ∉ S.1) (hb : b ∉ S.1) : S.restIndex p + 2 ≤ l := by
  have hsub : insert a (insert b {x ∈ S.1ᶜ | x < p}) ⊆ S.1ᶜ := by
    intro x
    simp only [mem_insert, mem_filter, mem_compl]
    rintro (rfl | rfl | ⟨hx, -⟩) <;> assumption
  have hcard := card_le_card hsub
  rw [card_insert_of_notMem, card_insert_of_notMem, card_compl, Fintype.card_fin, S.2] at hcard
  · unfold restIndex
    omega
  · simp only [mem_filter, not_and, not_lt]
    exact fun _ ↦ hpa.trans hab.le
  · simp only [mem_insert, mem_filter, not_or, not_and, not_lt]
    exact ⟨hab.ne, fun _ ↦ hpa⟩

/-- Between two rest positions and a later position, the number of rest positions increases by
at least two. -/
theorem restIndex_add_two_le_restIndex {S : ShuffleMask k l} {a b c : Fin (k + l)} (hab : a < b)
    (hbc : b < c) (ha : a ∉ S.1) (hb : b ∉ S.1) : S.restIndex a + 2 ≤ S.restIndex c := by
  have hsub : insert a (insert b {x ∈ S.1ᶜ | x < a}) ⊆ {x ∈ S.1ᶜ | x < c} := by
    intro x
    simp only [mem_insert, mem_filter, mem_compl]
    rintro (rfl | rfl | ⟨hx, hxa⟩)
    · exact ⟨ha, hab.trans hbc⟩
    · exact ⟨hb, hbc⟩
    · exact ⟨hx, hxa.trans (hab.trans hbc)⟩
  have hcard := card_le_card hsub
  rw [card_insert_of_notMem, card_insert_of_notMem] at hcard
  · exact hcard
  · simp [hab.not_gt]
  · simp [hab.ne]

/-- The initial mask, selecting the first `k` positions. -/
def initial : ShuffleMask k l :=
  ⟨({x | (x : ℕ) < k} : Finset (Fin (k + l))), by rw [Fin.card_filter_val_lt]; omega⟩

/-- The selected positions of the initial mask are those less than `k`. -/
@[simp]
theorem mem_initial {x : Fin (k + l)} : x ∈ (initial : ShuffleMask k l).1 ↔ (x : ℕ) < k := by
  simp [initial]

/-- In the initial mask, the rest position `p` is the `(p - k)`-th rest position, and there are
no rest positions before a selected position. -/
theorem restIndex_initial (p : Fin (k + l)) :
    (initial : ShuffleMask k l).restIndex p = p - k := by
  rcases lt_or_ge (p : ℕ) k with hp | hp
  · rw [restIndex, Nat.sub_eq_zero_of_le hp.le, card_eq_zero, filter_eq_empty_iff]
    intro x
    simp only [mem_compl, mem_initial, not_lt, Fin.lt_def]
    omega
  have h : ({x ∈ (initial : ShuffleMask k l).1ᶜ | x < p} : Finset (Fin (k + l))) =
      ({x | (x : ℕ) < p} : Finset (Fin (k + l))) \ ({x | (x : ℕ) < k} : Finset (Fin (k + l))) := by
    ext x
    simp only [mem_filter, mem_compl, mem_initial, mem_sdiff, mem_univ, true_and, Fin.lt_def]
    omega
  rw [restIndex, h, card_sdiff_of_subset, Fin.card_filter_val_lt, Fin.card_filter_val_lt]
  · omega
  · intro x
    simp only [mem_filter, mem_univ, true_and]
    omega

/-- An index for the generators of the Hecke algebra on the rest positions: the number of rest
positions before the first of two rest positions is less than `l - 1`. -/
theorem restIndex_lt_sub_one {S : ShuffleMask k l} {a b : Fin (k + l)} (hab : a < b)
    (ha : a ∉ S.1) (hb : b ∉ S.1) : S.restIndex a < l - 1 := by
  have := restIndex_add_two_le hab le_rfl ha hb
  omega

/-- The **length** of a mask `S`: the number of pairs of a rest position and a later selected
position. It is the length of the shortest permutation of the positions carrying the initial mask
onto `S`, the minimal-length representative of the coset of `S_k × S_l` in `S_(k + l)`
indexed by `S`; that identification is not needed here. -/
def length (S : ShuffleMask k l) : ℕ := ∑ s ∈ S.1, S.restIndex s

/-- The length of `S` adds up, over the selected positions, the number of rest positions before
them. -/
theorem length_def (S : ShuffleMask k l) : S.length = ∑ s ∈ S.1, S.restIndex s := (rfl)

/-- The initial mask has length `0`. -/
@[simp]
theorem length_initial : (initial : ShuffleMask k l).length = 0 :=
  Finset.sum_eq_zero fun s hs ↦ by
    rw [restIndex_initial, Nat.sub_eq_zero_of_le (mem_initial.1 hs).le]

/-- Moving a selected position back past the rest position just before it lowers the length by
one. -/
theorem length_swap_add_one_of_notMem_of_mem {S : ShuffleMask k l} {a b : Fin (k + l)}
    (hab : (b : ℕ) = a + 1) (ha : a ∉ S.1) (hb : b ∈ S.1) : (S.swap a b).length + 1 = S.length := by
  -- The selected positions of `S.swap a b` are by definition the image of those of `S`.
  have hsum : (S.swap a b).length = ∑ y ∈ S.1, (S.swap a b).restIndex (Equiv.swap a b y) :=
    Finset.sum_map _ _ _
  have hrest : ∑ y ∈ S.1.erase b, (S.swap a b).restIndex (Equiv.swap a b y) =
      ∑ y ∈ S.1.erase b, S.restIndex y := by
    refine Finset.sum_congr rfl fun y hy ↦ ?_
    obtain ⟨hyb, hy⟩ := Finset.mem_erase.1 hy
    have hya : y ≠ a := fun h ↦ ha (h ▸ hy)
    rw [Equiv.swap_apply_of_ne_of_ne hya hyb, restIndex_swap]
    have := Fin.val_ne_of_ne hya
    have := Fin.val_ne_of_ne hyb
    simp only [Fin.lt_def]
    omega
  rw [hsum, length_def, ← Finset.add_sum_erase _ _ hb, ← Finset.add_sum_erase _ _ hb, hrest,
    Equiv.swap_apply_right, restIndex_swap (by simp [Fin.lt_def, hab]),
    restIndex_of_notMem hab ha]
  omega

/-- Moving a selected position forward past the rest position just after it raises the length by
one. -/
theorem length_swap_of_mem_of_notMem {S : ShuffleMask k l} {a b : Fin (k + l)}
    (hab : (b : ℕ) = a + 1) (ha : a ∈ S.1) (hb : b ∉ S.1) :
    (S.swap a b).length = S.length + 1 := by
  have := length_swap_add_one_of_notMem_of_mem (S := S.swap a b) hab (by simpa using hb)
    (by simpa using ha)
  rw [swap_swap] at this
  omega

/-- A mask other than the initial one has a rest position directly followed by a selected
position. -/
theorem exists_notMem_mem_of_ne_initial {S : ShuffleMask k l} (hS : S ≠ initial) :
    ∃ a b : Fin (k + l), (b : ℕ) = a + 1 ∧ a ∉ S.1 ∧ b ∈ S.1 := by
  by_contra! H
  -- Otherwise the selected positions are closed downwards, so they are the first `k` positions.
  have hdown (d : ℕ) : ∀ x y : Fin (k + l), (x : ℕ) = y + d → x ∈ S.1 → y ∈ S.1 := by
    induction d with
    | zero => exact fun x y h hx ↦ Fin.ext h ▸ hx
    | succ d ih =>
      refine fun x y h hx ↦ ih ⟨y + d, by omega⟩ y rfl (not_not.1 fun h' ↦ H _ x ?_ h' hx)
      simp only
      omega
  refine hS (Subtype.ext (eq_of_subset_of_card_le (fun x hx ↦ ?_) (by rw [S.2, initial.2])))
  have hsub : ({y | (y : ℕ) < x + 1} : Finset (Fin (k + l))) ⊆ S.1 := fun y hy ↦
    hdown (x - y) x y (by simp only [mem_filter, mem_univ, true_and] at hy; omega) hx
  have := card_le_card hsub
  rw [Fin.card_filter_val_lt, S.2] at this
  rw [mem_initial]
  omega

/-- Only the initial mask has length `0`. -/
@[simp]
theorem length_eq_zero_iff {S : ShuffleMask k l} : S.length = 0 ↔ S = initial := by
  refine ⟨fun h ↦ by_contra fun hS ↦ ?_, fun h ↦ h ▸ length_initial⟩
  obtain ⟨a, b, hab, ha, hb⟩ := exists_notMem_mem_of_ne_initial hS
  have := length_swap_add_one_of_notMem_of_mem hab ha hb
  omega

/-- `IsShufflePath w S` says that the word `w` in the generator indices moves the initial mask to
`S` one step at a time: reading `w` from its last letter to its head, each letter `i` moves a
selected position `i` forward past the rest position `i + 1`. Every mask is reached
(`TauCeti.TypeAHeckeAlgebra.ShuffleMask.exists_isShufflePath`), and only by words of its length
(`TauCeti.TypeAHeckeAlgebra.ShuffleMask.IsShufflePath.length_eq`). Such words are the reduced
words of the minimal-length representatives of the cosets of `S_k × S_l` in `S_(k + l)`; that
identification is not needed here. -/
inductive IsShufflePath : List (Fin (k + l - 1)) → ShuffleMask k l → Prop
  /-- The empty word reaches the initial mask. -/
  | nil : IsShufflePath [] initial
  /-- A word reaching `S`, followed by a step moving a selected position `i` past the rest
  position `i + 1`. -/
  | cons {w : List (Fin (k + l - 1))} {S : ShuffleMask k l} {i : Fin (k + l - 1)}
      (h : IsShufflePath w S) (ha : BraidGroup.strand i ∈ S.1)
      (hb : BraidGroup.strandSucc i ∉ S.1) :
      IsShufflePath (i :: w) (S.swap (BraidGroup.strand i) (BraidGroup.strandSucc i))

/-- A shuffle path to `S` has `S.length` letters. -/
theorem IsShufflePath.length_eq {w : List (Fin (k + l - 1))} {S : ShuffleMask k l}
    (h : IsShufflePath w S) : w.length = S.length := by
  induction h with
  | nil => simp
  | cons _ ha hb ih => rw [List.length_cons, ih, length_swap_of_mem_of_notMem (by simp) ha hb]

/-- Every mask is reached by a shuffle path. -/
theorem exists_isShufflePath (S : ShuffleMask k l) : ∃ w, IsShufflePath w S := by
  induction hn : S.length generalizing S with
  | zero => exact ⟨[], length_eq_zero_iff.1 hn ▸ .nil⟩
  | succ n ih =>
    obtain ⟨a, b, hab, ha, hb⟩ :=
      exists_notMem_mem_of_ne_initial (S := S) (by rintro rfl; simp at hn)
    obtain ⟨w, hw⟩ :=
      ih (S.swap a b) (by have := length_swap_add_one_of_notMem_of_mem hab ha hb; omega)
    obtain ⟨i, rfl, rfl⟩ : ∃ i : Fin (k + l - 1),
        BraidGroup.strand i = a ∧ BraidGroup.strandSucc i = b :=
      ⟨⟨a, by have := b.isLt; omega⟩, Fin.ext (BraidGroup.val_strand _),
        Fin.ext ((BraidGroup.val_strandSucc _).trans hab.symm)⟩
    exact ⟨i :: w, by simpa using hw.cons (i := i) (by simpa using hb) (by simpa using ha)⟩

end ShuffleMask

variable {R : Type*} [CommRing R] {q : Rˣ} {U : Type*} [AddCommGroup U] [Module R U]

section Operators

variable (ρ : TypeAHeckeAlgebra R q l →ₐ[R] Module.End R U)

/-- The generator `T r` of the Hecke algebra on the rest positions, acting on `U`; it is `0` when
`r` is out of range, which never happens on two adjacent rest positions. -/
private noncomputable def restT (r : ℕ) : Module.End R U :=
  if h : r < l - 1 then ρ (T q ⟨r, h⟩) else 0

private theorem restT_of_lt {r : ℕ} (h : r < l - 1) : restT ρ r = ρ (T q ⟨r, h⟩) := by
  simp only [restT, h, ↓reduceDIte]

private theorem restT_restT {r : ℕ} (h : r < l - 1) (u : U) :
    restT ρ r (restT ρ r u) = ((q : R) - ↑q⁻¹) • restT ρ r u + u := by
  rw [restT_of_lt ρ h, ← mul_apply_eq_comp, ← map_mul, T_mul_self]
  simp

private theorem restT_braid {r : ℕ} (h : r + 1 < l - 1) (u : U) :
    restT ρ r (restT ρ (r + 1) (restT ρ r u)) =
      restT ρ (r + 1) (restT ρ r (restT ρ (r + 1) u)) := by
  rw [restT_of_lt ρ h, restT_of_lt ρ (by omega : r < l - 1)]
  simp only [← mul_apply_eq_comp, ← map_mul, ← mul_assoc]
  rw [T_braid (Or.inl rfl)]

private theorem restT_comm {r r' : ℕ} (h : r + 2 ≤ r') (h' : r' < l - 1) (u : U) :
    restT ρ r (restT ρ r' u) = restT ρ r' (restT ρ r u) := by
  rw [restT_of_lt ρ h', restT_of_lt ρ (by omega : r < l - 1)]
  simp only [← mul_apply_eq_comp, ← map_mul]
  rw [(commute_T (Or.inl h)).eq]

/-- The operator of the shuffle module crossing the positions `a` and `b`. -/
private noncomputable def shuffleOp (a b : Fin (k + l)) :
    Module.End R (ShuffleMask k l → U) where
  toFun f S :=
    if a ∈ S.1 then
      if b ∈ S.1 then (q : R) • f S else ((q : R) - ↑q⁻¹) • f S - f (S.swap a b)
    else if b ∈ S.1 then -f (S.swap a b) else restT ρ (S.restIndex a) (f S)
  map_add' f g := by
    ext S
    simp only [Pi.add_apply, map_add]
    split_ifs <;> module
  map_smul' c f := by
    ext S
    simp only [Pi.smul_apply, map_smul, RingHom.id_apply]
    split_ifs <;> module

private theorem shuffleOp_apply (a b : Fin (k + l)) (f : ShuffleMask k l → U)
    (S : ShuffleMask k l) :
    shuffleOp ρ a b f S =
      if a ∈ S.1 then
        if b ∈ S.1 then (q : R) • f S else ((q : R) - ↑q⁻¹) • f S - f (S.swap a b)
      else if b ∈ S.1 then -f (S.swap a b) else restT ρ (S.restIndex a) (f S) := (rfl)

private theorem shuffleOp_mul_self {a b : Fin (k + l)} (hab : (b : ℕ) = a + 1) :
    shuffleOp ρ a b * shuffleOp ρ a b = ((q : R) - ↑q⁻¹) • shuffleOp ρ a b + 1 := by
  have hlt : a < b := by rw [Fin.lt_def]; omega
  refine LinearMap.ext fun f ↦ funext fun S ↦ ?_
  simp only [mul_apply_eq_comp, LinearMap.add_apply, LinearMap.smul_apply,
    one_apply_eq_self, Pi.add_apply, Pi.smul_apply, shuffleOp_apply]
  by_cases ha : a ∈ S.1 <;> by_cases hb : b ∈ S.1 <;>
    simp only [ha, hb, ShuffleMask.mem_swap, Equiv.swap_apply_left, Equiv.swap_apply_right,
      ShuffleMask.swap_swap, ↓reduceIte]
  · have hq : (q : R) * q = ((q : R) - ↑q⁻¹) * q + 1 := by
      rw [sub_mul, Units.inv_mul]; ring
    rw [smul_smul, hq, add_smul, one_smul, mul_smul]
  · module
  · module
  · rw [restT_restT ρ (by have := ShuffleMask.restIndex_add_two_le hlt le_rfl ha hb; omega)]

private theorem shuffleOp_braid {a b c : Fin (k + l)} (hab : (b : ℕ) = a + 1)
    (hbc : (c : ℕ) = b + 1) :
    shuffleOp ρ a b * shuffleOp ρ b c * shuffleOp ρ a b =
      shuffleOp ρ b c * shuffleOp ρ a b * shuffleOp ρ b c := by
  have hab' : a < b := by rw [Fin.lt_def]; omega
  have hbc' : b < c := by rw [Fin.lt_def]; omega
  have hac : a ≠ c := by rw [ne_eq, Fin.ext_iff]; omega
  have h₁ (M : ShuffleMask k l) (h : a ∈ M.1) : M.restIndex b = M.restIndex a :=
    ShuffleMask.restIndex_of_mem hab h
  have h₂ (M : ShuffleMask k l) (h : a ∉ M.1) : M.restIndex b = M.restIndex a + 1 :=
    ShuffleMask.restIndex_of_notMem hab h
  have h₃ (M : ShuffleMask k l) : (M.swap a b).restIndex a = M.restIndex a :=
    ShuffleMask.restIndex_swap (by simp [hab'.not_gt])
  have h₄ (M : ShuffleMask k l) : (M.swap b c).restIndex a = M.restIndex a :=
    ShuffleMask.restIndex_swap (by simp [hab'.not_gt, (hab'.trans hbc').not_gt])
  refine LinearMap.ext fun f ↦ funext fun S ↦ ?_
  simp only [mul_apply_eq_comp, shuffleOp_apply]
  by_cases ha : a ∈ S.1 <;> by_cases hb : b ∈ S.1 <;> by_cases hc : c ∈ S.1 <;>
    simp only [ha, hb, hc, ShuffleMask.mem_swap, Equiv.swap_apply_left, Equiv.swap_apply_right,
      Equiv.swap_apply_of_ne_of_ne, hab'.ne, hbc'.ne', hac, hac.symm,
      ShuffleMask.swap_swap, ↓reduceIte, h₁, h₂, h₃, h₄, map_sub, map_smul, map_neg, ne_eq,
      not_false_eq_true]
  -- The cases `(1, 1, 1)` and `(0, 0, 1)` of membership of `a, b, c` are closed by `simp`.
  · match_scalars
    · linear_combination ((q : R) - ↑q⁻¹) * Units.mul_inv q
    all_goals ring
  · module
  · rw [restT_restT ρ (by have := ShuffleMask.restIndex_add_two_le hbc' hab'.le hb hc; omega)]
    module
  · module
  · module
  · exact restT_braid ρ
      (by have := ShuffleMask.restIndex_add_two_le hbc' le_rfl hb hc; have := h₂ S ha; omega) _

private theorem shuffleOp_comm {a b c d : Fin (k + l)} (hab : (b : ℕ) = a + 1)
    (hbc : (b : ℕ) < c) (hcd : (d : ℕ) = c + 1) :
    shuffleOp ρ a b * shuffleOp ρ c d = shuffleOp ρ c d * shuffleOp ρ a b := by
  have hab' : a < b := by rw [Fin.lt_def]; omega
  have hbc' : b < c := by rw [Fin.lt_def]; omega
  have hcd' : c < d := by rw [Fin.lt_def]; omega
  have hac : a ≠ c := by rw [ne_eq, Fin.ext_iff]; omega
  have had : a ≠ d := by rw [ne_eq, Fin.ext_iff]; omega
  have hbd : b ≠ d := by rw [ne_eq, Fin.ext_iff]; omega
  have h₁ (M : ShuffleMask k l) : (M.swap a b).restIndex c = M.restIndex c :=
    ShuffleMask.restIndex_swap (by simp [hab'.trans hbc', hbc'])
  have h₂ (M : ShuffleMask k l) : (M.swap c d).restIndex a = M.restIndex a :=
    ShuffleMask.restIndex_swap
      (by simp [(hab'.trans hbc').not_gt, (hab'.trans (hbc'.trans hcd')).not_gt])
  have h₃ (M : ShuffleMask k l) : (M.swap c d).swap a b = (M.swap a b).swap c d := by
    refine Subtype.ext <| Finset.ext fun x ↦ ?_
    have hcomm := (Equiv.Perm.disjoint_swap_swap
      (by simp [hab'.ne, hac, had, hbc'.ne, hbd, hcd'.ne] : [a, b, c, d].Nodup)).commute
    simp only [ShuffleMask.mem_swap, ← Equiv.Perm.mul_apply, hcomm.eq]
  refine LinearMap.ext fun f ↦ funext fun S ↦ ?_
  simp only [mul_apply_eq_comp, shuffleOp_apply]
  by_cases ha : a ∈ S.1 <;> by_cases hb : b ∈ S.1 <;> by_cases hc : c ∈ S.1 <;>
    by_cases hd : d ∈ S.1 <;>
    simp only [ha, hb, hc, hd, ShuffleMask.mem_swap, Equiv.swap_apply_of_ne_of_ne, hac, had, hbd,
      hbc'.ne, hac.symm, had.symm, hbd.symm, hbc'.ne', h₁, h₂, h₃, ↓reduceIte, map_sub, map_smul,
      map_neg, ne_eq, not_false_eq_true]
  all_goals first
    | module
    | exact restT_comm ρ (ShuffleMask.restIndex_add_two_le_restIndex hab' hbc' ha hb)
        (by have := ShuffleMask.restIndex_add_two_le hcd' le_rfl hc hd; omega) _

end Operators

section Rep

variable (k) (ρ : TypeAHeckeAlgebra R q l →ₐ[R] Module.End R U)

/-- The **shuffle module** `Sh_k(U)` of a module `U` over the Hecke algebra on `l` strands: the
representation of the Hecke algebra on `k + l` strands on the functions from the masks to `U`, in
which `T i` multiplies by `q` on two selected positions, acts on `U` through `ρ` on two rest
positions, and acts by `[[q - q⁻¹, -1], [-1, 0]]` on a selected and a rest position. -/
noncomputable def shuffleRep :
    TypeAHeckeAlgebra R q (k + l) →ₐ[R] Module.End R (ShuffleMask k l → U) :=
  lift (fun i ↦ shuffleOp ρ (BraidGroup.strand i) (BraidGroup.strandSucc i))
    (fun _ ↦ shuffleOp_mul_self ρ (by simp))
    (fun h ↦ by
      rw [BraidGroup.strand_eq_strandSucc_of_succ h]
      exact shuffleOp_braid ρ (by simp) (by simp [← h]))
    (fun h ↦ shuffleOp_comm ρ (by simp) (by simp; omega) (by simp))

variable {k}

private theorem shuffleRep_T (i : Fin (k + l - 1)) :
    shuffleRep k ρ (T q i) = shuffleOp ρ (BraidGroup.strand i) (BraidGroup.strandSucc i) := by
  rw [shuffleRep, lift_T]

/-- At a mask selecting both positions crossed by `T i`, the generator multiplies the value
by `q`. -/
@[simp]
theorem shuffleRep_T_apply_of_mem_of_mem {i : Fin (k + l - 1)} {S : ShuffleMask k l}
    (ha : BraidGroup.strand i ∈ S.1) (hb : BraidGroup.strandSucc i ∈ S.1)
    (f : ShuffleMask k l → U) : shuffleRep k ρ (T q i) f S = (q : R) • f S := by
  simp [shuffleRep_T, shuffleOp_apply, ha, hb]

/-- At a mask selecting the first but not the second position crossed by `T i`, the value of
`T i • f` is `(q - q⁻¹) • f S - f S'`, where `S'` exchanges the two positions. -/
@[simp]
theorem shuffleRep_T_apply_of_mem_of_notMem {i : Fin (k + l - 1)} {S : ShuffleMask k l}
    (ha : BraidGroup.strand i ∈ S.1) (hb : BraidGroup.strandSucc i ∉ S.1)
    (f : ShuffleMask k l → U) :
    shuffleRep k ρ (T q i) f S =
      ((q : R) - ↑q⁻¹) • f S - f (S.swap (BraidGroup.strand i) (BraidGroup.strandSucc i)) := by
  simp [shuffleRep_T, shuffleOp_apply, ha, hb]

/-- At a mask selecting the second but not the first position crossed by `T i`, the value of
`T i • f` is `-f S'`, where `S'` exchanges the two positions. -/
@[simp]
theorem shuffleRep_T_apply_of_notMem_of_mem {i : Fin (k + l - 1)} {S : ShuffleMask k l}
    (ha : BraidGroup.strand i ∉ S.1) (hb : BraidGroup.strandSucc i ∈ S.1)
    (f : ShuffleMask k l → U) :
    shuffleRep k ρ (T q i) f S = -f (S.swap (BraidGroup.strand i) (BraidGroup.strandSucc i)) := by
  simp [shuffleRep_T, shuffleOp_apply, ha, hb]

/-- At a mask selecting neither position crossed by `T i`, the generator acts on the value by the
generator of `H_l` indexed by the position of the first of them among the rest positions. -/
@[simp]
theorem shuffleRep_T_apply_of_notMem_of_notMem {i : Fin (k + l - 1)} {S : ShuffleMask k l}
    (ha : BraidGroup.strand i ∉ S.1) (hb : BraidGroup.strandSucc i ∉ S.1)
    (f : ShuffleMask k l → U) :
    shuffleRep k ρ (T q i) f S =
      ρ (T q ⟨S.restIndex (BraidGroup.strand i),
        ShuffleMask.restIndex_lt_sub_one (by simp [Fin.lt_def]) ha hb⟩) (f S) := by
  simp only [shuffleRep_T, shuffleOp_apply, ha, hb, ↓reduceIte]
  rw [restT_of_lt]

variable {ρ} in
/-- **Naturality in the rest module.** A linear map of rest modules commuting with the generators
of `H_l`, applied at every mask, commutes with the shuffle modules. -/
theorem compLeft_comp_shuffleRep {V : Type*} [AddCommGroup V] [Module R V]
    {ρ' : TypeAHeckeAlgebra R q l →ₐ[R] Module.End R V} (φ : U →ₗ[R] V)
    (hφ : ∀ i, φ ∘ₗ ρ (T q i) = ρ' (T q i) ∘ₗ φ) (x : TypeAHeckeAlgebra R q (k + l)) :
    φ.compLeft (ShuffleMask k l) ∘ₗ shuffleRep k ρ x =
      shuffleRep k ρ' x ∘ₗ φ.compLeft (ShuffleMask k l) := by
  have hrest (r : ℕ) (u : U) : φ (restT ρ r u) = restT ρ' r (φ u) := by
    unfold restT
    split_ifs with h
    · exact LinearMap.congr_fun (hφ ⟨r, h⟩) u
    · simp
  have hx : x ∈ Algebra.adjoin R (Set.range (T (n := k + l) q)) := by
    rw [adjoin_range_T]
    trivial
  induction hx using Algebra.adjoin_induction with
  | mem x hx =>
    obtain ⟨i, rfl⟩ := hx
    refine LinearMap.ext fun f ↦ funext fun S ↦ ?_
    simp only [LinearMap.comp_apply, LinearMap.compLeft_apply, Function.comp_apply, shuffleRep_T,
      shuffleOp_apply]
    split_ifs <;> simp [hrest]
  | algebraMap r =>
    ext
    simp
  | add x y _ _ hx hy => rw [map_add, map_add, LinearMap.comp_add, LinearMap.add_comp, hx, hy]
  | mul x y _ _ hx hy =>
    rw [map_mul, map_mul, Module.End.mul_eq_comp, Module.End.mul_eq_comp, ← LinearMap.comp_assoc,
      hx, LinearMap.comp_assoc, hy, LinearMap.comp_assoc]

/-- A generator crossing two positions on the same side of the initial mask kills the functions
supported at the initial mask everywhere else. -/
private theorem shuffleRep_T_single_initial_of_ne {i : Fin (k + l - 1)}
    (h : BraidGroup.strand i ∈ (ShuffleMask.initial : ShuffleMask k l).1 ↔
      BraidGroup.strandSucc i ∈ (ShuffleMask.initial : ShuffleMask k l).1)
    (u : U) {S : ShuffleMask k l} (hS : S ≠ ShuffleMask.initial) :
    shuffleRep k ρ (T q i) (Pi.single ShuffleMask.initial u) S = 0 := by
  have hswap (hS' : S.swap (BraidGroup.strand i) (BraidGroup.strandSucc i) = ShuffleMask.initial) :
      (BraidGroup.strand i ∈ S.1 ↔ BraidGroup.strandSucc i ∈ S.1) := by
    rw [← hS'] at h
    simpa [Equiv.swap_apply_left, Equiv.swap_apply_right, Iff.comm] using h
  simp only [shuffleRep_T, shuffleOp_apply]
  split_ifs with ha hb hb <;>
    simp only [Pi.single_eq_of_ne hS, smul_zero, map_zero, zero_sub, neg_eq_zero]
  · exact Pi.single_eq_of_ne (fun h' ↦ hb ((hswap h').1 ha)) _
  · exact Pi.single_eq_of_ne (fun h' ↦ ha ((hswap h').2 hb)) _

/-- On the functions supported at the initial mask, a generator crossing two selected positions
acts by `q`. -/
theorem shuffleRep_T_single_initial_of_lt {i : Fin (k + l - 1)} (hi : (i : ℕ) + 1 < k) (u : U) :
    shuffleRep k ρ (T q i) (Pi.single ShuffleMask.initial u) =
      (q : R) • Pi.single ShuffleMask.initial u := by
  ext S
  by_cases hS : S = ShuffleMask.initial
  · subst hS
    rw [shuffleRep_T_apply_of_mem_of_mem ρ (by simp; omega) (by simp; omega), Pi.smul_apply]
  · rw [shuffleRep_T_single_initial_of_ne ρ (by simp; omega) u hS, Pi.smul_apply,
      Pi.single_eq_of_ne hS, smul_zero]

/-- On the functions supported at the initial mask, the generator crossing the rest positions
`k + j` and `k + j + 1` acts on `U` by the generator `T j` of `H_l`. -/
theorem shuffleRep_T_add_single_initial (j : Fin (l - 1)) (u : U) :
    shuffleRep k ρ (T q ⟨k + j, by omega⟩) (Pi.single ShuffleMask.initial u) =
      Pi.single ShuffleMask.initial (ρ (T q j) u) := by
  ext S
  by_cases hS : S = ShuffleMask.initial
  · subst hS
    rw [shuffleRep_T_apply_of_notMem_of_notMem ρ (by simp) (by simp; omega)]
    simp only [Pi.single_eq_same]
    congr 3
    ext
    simp [ShuffleMask.restIndex_initial]
  · rw [shuffleRep_T_single_initial_of_ne ρ (by simp; omega) u hS, Pi.single_eq_of_ne hS]

/-- A generator sends the vector at `S` to a function vanishing outside `S` and the mask
exchanging the two positions it crosses. -/
private theorem shuffleRep_T_single_apply_of_ne {i : Fin (k + l - 1)} {S M : ShuffleMask k l}
    (hM : M ≠ S) (hM' : M ≠ S.swap (BraidGroup.strand i) (BraidGroup.strandSucc i)) (u : U) :
    shuffleRep k ρ (T q i) (Pi.single S u) M = 0 := by
  have hM'' : M.swap (BraidGroup.strand i) (BraidGroup.strandSucc i) ≠ S := by
    rwa [ne_eq, Function.Involutive.eq_iff (ShuffleMask.swap_swap _ _)]
  simp only [shuffleRep_T, shuffleOp_apply, Pi.single_eq_of_ne hM, Pi.single_eq_of_ne hM'']
  split_ifs <;> simp

/-- At a mask selecting the first but not the second position crossed by `T i`, the generator
sends the vector `u` at `S` to `(q - q⁻¹) • u` at `S` minus `u` at the exchanged mask. -/
theorem shuffleRep_T_single_of_mem_of_notMem {i : Fin (k + l - 1)} {S : ShuffleMask k l}
    (ha : BraidGroup.strand i ∈ S.1) (hb : BraidGroup.strandSucc i ∉ S.1) (u : U) :
    shuffleRep k ρ (T q i) (Pi.single S u) =
      ((q : R) - ↑q⁻¹) • (Pi.single S u : ShuffleMask k l → U) -
        Pi.single (S.swap (BraidGroup.strand i) (BraidGroup.strandSucc i)) u := by
  have hne : S.swap (BraidGroup.strand i) (BraidGroup.strandSucc i) ≠ S := fun h ↦
    hb (by rw [← h] at ha; simpa using ha)
  ext M
  by_cases hM : M = S
  · subst hM
    rw [shuffleRep_T_apply_of_mem_of_notMem ρ ha hb]
    simp [Pi.single_eq_of_ne hne, Pi.single_eq_of_ne hne.symm]
  by_cases hM' : M = S.swap (BraidGroup.strand i) (BraidGroup.strandSucc i)
  · subst hM'
    rw [shuffleRep_T_apply_of_notMem_of_mem ρ (by simpa using hb) (by simpa using ha)]
    simp [Pi.single_eq_of_ne hne]
  · simp [shuffleRep_T_single_apply_of_ne ρ hM hM', Pi.single_eq_of_ne hM, Pi.single_eq_of_ne hM']

/-- At a mask selecting the second but not the first position crossed by `T i`, the generator
sends the vector `u` at `S` to `-u` at the exchanged mask. -/
theorem shuffleRep_T_single_of_notMem_of_mem {i : Fin (k + l - 1)} {S : ShuffleMask k l}
    (ha : BraidGroup.strand i ∉ S.1) (hb : BraidGroup.strandSucc i ∈ S.1) (u : U) :
    shuffleRep k ρ (T q i) (Pi.single S u) =
      -Pi.single (S.swap (BraidGroup.strand i) (BraidGroup.strandSucc i)) u := by
  have hne : S.swap (BraidGroup.strand i) (BraidGroup.strandSucc i) ≠ S := fun h ↦
    ha (by rw [← h] at hb; simpa using hb)
  ext M
  by_cases hM : M = S
  · subst hM
    rw [shuffleRep_T_apply_of_notMem_of_mem ρ ha hb]
    simp [Pi.single_eq_of_ne hne, Pi.single_eq_of_ne hne.symm]
  by_cases hM' : M = S.swap (BraidGroup.strand i) (BraidGroup.strandSucc i)
  · subst hM'
    rw [shuffleRep_T_apply_of_mem_of_notMem ρ (by simpa using hb) (by simpa using ha)]
    simp [Pi.single_eq_of_ne hne]
  · simp [shuffleRep_T_single_apply_of_ne ρ hM hM', Pi.single_eq_of_ne hM']

/-- At a mask selecting the first but not the second position crossed by `T i`, the inverse
generator sends the vector `u` at `S` to `-u` at the exchanged mask. -/
theorem shuffleRep_val_inv_unitT_single_of_mem_of_notMem {i : Fin (k + l - 1)}
    {S : ShuffleMask k l} (ha : BraidGroup.strand i ∈ S.1) (hb : BraidGroup.strandSucc i ∉ S.1)
    (u : U) :
    shuffleRep k ρ ↑(unitT q i)⁻¹ (Pi.single S u) =
      -Pi.single (S.swap (BraidGroup.strand i) (BraidGroup.strandSucc i)) u := by
  rw [val_inv_unitT, map_sub, AlgHom.commutes, LinearMap.sub_apply,
    shuffleRep_T_single_of_mem_of_notMem ρ ha hb, Module.algebraMap_end_apply]
  abel

/-- **Inverse shuffle words are monomial on the initial mask.** Along a shuffle path `w` to `S`,
the product of the inverse generators sends the vector `u` at the initial mask to
`(-1) ^ S.length • u` at `S`. -/
theorem ShuffleMask.IsShufflePath.shuffleRep_prod_val_inv_unitT_single_initial
    {w : List (Fin (k + l - 1))} {S : ShuffleMask k l} (h : ShuffleMask.IsShufflePath w S)
    (u : U) :
    shuffleRep k ρ (w.map fun i ↦ (↑(unitT q i)⁻¹ : TypeAHeckeAlgebra R q (k + l))).prod
        (Pi.single ShuffleMask.initial u) =
      (-1 : R) ^ S.length • Pi.single S u := by
  induction h with
  | nil => simp
  | cons _ ha hb ih =>
    rw [List.map_cons, List.prod_cons, map_mul, mul_apply_eq_comp, ih, map_smul,
      shuffleRep_val_inv_unitT_single_of_mem_of_notMem ρ ha hb,
      ShuffleMask.length_swap_of_mem_of_notMem (by simp) ha hb, pow_succ, mul_neg_one, neg_smul,
      smul_neg]

/-- The shuffle-path triangularity, in one statement: along a shuffle path `w` to `S`, the
product of the generators sends the vector `u` at the initial mask to a function whose value at
`S` is `(-1) ^ S.length • u` and which vanishes at every other mask of length at least
`S.length`. -/
private theorem ShuffleMask.IsShufflePath.shuffleRep_prod_T_single_initial
    {w : List (Fin (k + l - 1))} {S : ShuffleMask k l} (h : ShuffleMask.IsShufflePath w S)
    (u : U) :
    shuffleRep k ρ (w.map (T q)).prod (Pi.single ShuffleMask.initial u) S =
        (-1 : R) ^ S.length • u ∧
      ∀ M : ShuffleMask k l, S.length ≤ M.length → M ≠ S →
        shuffleRep k ρ (w.map (T q)).prod (Pi.single ShuffleMask.initial u) M = 0 := by
  induction h with
  | nil =>
    refine ⟨by simp, fun M _ hM ↦ ?_⟩
    simp [Pi.single_eq_of_ne hM]
  | @cons w S i _ ha hb ih =>
    obtain ⟨ih₁, ih₂⟩ := ih
    have hab : (BraidGroup.strandSucc i : ℕ) = BraidGroup.strand i + 1 := by simp
    have hlen := ShuffleMask.length_swap_of_mem_of_notMem hab ha hb
    simp only [List.map_cons, List.prod_cons, map_mul, mul_apply_eq_comp, hlen]
    refine ⟨?_, fun M hM hne ↦ ?_⟩
    · rw [shuffleRep_T_apply_of_notMem_of_mem ρ (by simpa using hb) (by simpa using ha),
        ShuffleMask.swap_swap, ih₁, pow_succ, mul_neg_one, neg_smul]
    -- The value at `M` only involves the values at `M` and at the exchanged mask, both of which
    -- have length at least `S.length` and differ from `S`.
    have hM' : M ≠ S := by rintro rfl; omega
    have hswap : M.swap (BraidGroup.strand i) (BraidGroup.strandSucc i) ≠ S := by
      rwa [ne_eq, Function.Involutive.eq_iff (ShuffleMask.swap_swap _ _)]
    by_cases ha' : BraidGroup.strand i ∈ M.1 <;> by_cases hb' : BraidGroup.strandSucc i ∈ M.1
    · rw [shuffleRep_T_apply_of_mem_of_mem ρ ha' hb', ih₂ M (by omega) hM', smul_zero]
    · rw [shuffleRep_T_apply_of_mem_of_notMem ρ ha' hb', ih₂ M (by omega) hM',
        ih₂ _ (by rw [ShuffleMask.length_swap_of_mem_of_notMem hab ha' hb']; omega) hswap,
        smul_zero, sub_zero]
    · rw [shuffleRep_T_apply_of_notMem_of_mem ρ ha' hb',
        ih₂ _ (by have := ShuffleMask.length_swap_add_one_of_notMem_of_mem hab ha' hb'; omega)
          hswap, neg_zero]
    · rw [shuffleRep_T_apply_of_notMem_of_notMem ρ ha' hb', ih₂ M (by omega) hM', map_zero]

/-- **Triangularity of shuffle words**, leading coefficient: along a shuffle path `w` to `S`, the
product of the generators sends the vector `u` at the initial mask to a function with value
`(-1) ^ S.length • u` at `S`. -/
theorem ShuffleMask.IsShufflePath.shuffleRep_prod_T_single_initial_apply_self
    {w : List (Fin (k + l - 1))} {S : ShuffleMask k l} (h : ShuffleMask.IsShufflePath w S)
    (u : U) :
    shuffleRep k ρ (w.map (T q)).prod (Pi.single ShuffleMask.initial u) S =
      (-1 : R) ^ S.length • u :=
  (h.shuffleRep_prod_T_single_initial ρ u).1

/-- **Triangularity of shuffle words**, lower terms: along a shuffle path `w` to `S`, the product
of the generators sends the vector `u` at the initial mask to a function vanishing at every mask
other than `S` whose length is at least `S.length`. -/
theorem ShuffleMask.IsShufflePath.shuffleRep_prod_T_single_initial_apply_of_length_le
    {w : List (Fin (k + l - 1))} {S : ShuffleMask k l} (h : ShuffleMask.IsShufflePath w S)
    (u : U) {M : ShuffleMask k l} (hM : S.length ≤ M.length) (hne : M ≠ S) :
    shuffleRep k ρ (w.map (T q)).prod (Pi.single ShuffleMask.initial u) M = 0 :=
  (h.shuffleRep_prod_T_single_initial ρ u).2 M hM hne

/-- **The shuffle module is generated by its initial mask**: the images of the vectors at the
initial mask under the Hecke algebra on `k + l` strands span `Sh_k(U)`. -/
theorem span_range_shuffleRep_single_initial_eq_top :
    Submodule.span R (Set.range fun p : TypeAHeckeAlgebra R q (k + l) × U ↦
      shuffleRep k ρ p.1 (Pi.single ShuffleMask.initial p.2)) = ⊤ := by
  refine eq_top_iff.2 fun f _ ↦ ?_
  rw [← Finset.univ_sum_single f]
  refine Submodule.sum_mem _ fun S _ ↦ Submodule.subset_span ?_
  obtain ⟨w, hw⟩ := ShuffleMask.exists_isShufflePath S
  refine ⟨((-1 : R) ^ S.length •
    (w.map fun i ↦ (↑(unitT q i)⁻¹ : TypeAHeckeAlgebra R q (k + l))).prod, f S), ?_⟩
  simp only [map_smul, LinearMap.smul_apply, hw.shuffleRep_prod_val_inv_unitT_single_initial,
    smul_smul, ← mul_pow, neg_one_mul, neg_neg, one_pow, one_smul]

end Rep

end TauCeti.TypeAHeckeAlgebra
